ive\n\nAnything you test and find off — say which page and I'll fix it. If you'd like *more* demo meetings to poke at (a second deal, a noisy all-hands, a hiring loop), I can add those too."}
{"ts":"2026-10-24T03:49:32.439Z","session":"f6e804a3-1c28-4634-abd5-b0395560dade","response":"Done — you can now book meetings inside the app itself, live on prod (https://minutes-bharath-rs-projects.vercel.app).\n\n**How it works:**\n\n1. **Book** — click **\"Book a meeting\"** (top right of the meetings page) or go straight to `/book`. Pick the call type (sales discovery, team standup, one-on-one, or interview), give it a title, date/time, platform (Zoom / Meet / Teams / in person), capture mode, and attendee names.\n2. **Armed** — the booking lands in a \"Armed — booked in this browser\" list on your dashboard, alongside the seeded armed calls. Click it to preview the capture.\n3. **Record** — hit **\"Simulate the call starting\"** (or jump straight to the end with \"Jump to call end ⏭\"). The transcript streams in, the speaking graph grows, and when the call ends Minutes writes the summary and action items.\n4. **The full meeting** — \"Open the full meeting\" takes you to a completely generated recorded call: playback, cited summary, action items with dispatch (email/Jira draft → approve → toast), highlights, auto-clips, and \"Chat with the call\" — which answers with real quotes and `[mm:ss]` citations that seek the player. It appears in a \"Booked calls — completed here\" section with a \"Forget these\" button to wipe them.\n\n**One honest constraint:** with no database, booked meetings live in *your browser's* storage — they survive reloads, but only you see them, and the UI says so everywhere (booking pages from another browser will show \"This booking isn't in this browser\" instead of erroring). The seeded data is untouched.\n\nI ran the full click-through with Playwright — booking → armed → capture → recorded → all four features working on the generated meeting, with zero JS errors. Committed (`12f04cc`), pushed, and deployed; all routes verified 200 on prod and the deployment log is clean.\n\n**Try this path on prod:** Book a meeting → keep the defaults → submit → run the capture (real-time mode is fun, ~1 min; or jump to the end) → open the meeting → ask chat \"What about the latency work?\" if you booked an interview, or hit Dispatch on an action item.\n\nOne heads-up: production now also aliases to **https://minutes-jet.vercel.app** — both URLs serve the same app."}
