{"ts":"2026-10-24T04:06:04.853Z","session":"f6e804a3-1c28-4634-abd5-b0395560dade","response":"Booking is already in the app and live — built it a few steps ago, deployed at https://minutes-bharath-rs-projects.vercel.app/book. You can use it right now:\n\n**Where to find it:**\n- On the meetings page, top right: the black **\"Book a meeting\"** button\n- Or the direct link: `/book`\n\n**The flow, as built:**\n\n1. **Book it** — pick the meeting type (Sales discovery / Team standup / One-on-one / Interview), set the title, date, time, where (Zoom / Google Meet / Teams / in person), capture mode (bot joins / bot-free), and who's on the call. Hit **\"Book & arm the capture\"**.\n2. **It's armed** — the booking appears on your dashboard in \"Armed — booked in this browser\", alongside the seeded armed calls. Other people/attendees don't exist in this build, so it's yours only.\n3. **Record it** — click it to preview the capture, then **\"Simulate the call starting\"**. The transcript streams in live with the speaking graph growing (with a \"Jump to call end ⏭\" shortcut). When it ends, Minutes writes the summary and action items — and the meeting is recorded.\n4. **Use everything on it** — it shows up in \"Booked calls — completed here\" on your dashboard, opens as a full meeting (`/m/demo-…`) with playback, cited summary, dispatch (email/Jira → approve → toast), highlights, auto-clips, and chat that answers from its transcript with `[mm:ss]` citations.\n5. **Clean up** — \"Forget these\" on the dashboard wipes your bookings.\n\nOne honest constraint (labeled in the UI): booked meetings live in **your browser's storage** — no database, so they're yours only, and a booking opened from another browser shows \"This booking isn't in this browser\".\n\nIf you tried it and something didn't work, tell me what you hit — a step that failed, or where you expected it to appear. If you want a change — e.g., invite links for the \"attendees\", the booking appearing in the Search results, or a real database instead of localStorage — say the word and I'll build it."}
