{"ts":"2026-10-24T09:17:55.082Z","session":"f6e804a3-1c28-4634-abd5-b0395560dade","response":"Your send was accepted by Supabase (I just verified the project's auth config — email sign-in is on, sign-ups are on), so the bottleneck is on the email-delivery side, not the app. This is the known weak spot of the **built-in Supabase mailer on the free tier** — here's why and what to do:\n\n## Most likely causes, in order\n\n1. **It's in spam / Promotions.** The built-in mailer sends from a generic Supabase address that Gmail, Outlook and corporate mail frequently filter. Check spam, Promotions, and quarantine first — this is the #1 cause.\n2. **Rate limit ate a retry.** The built-in mailer allows only ~**2 emails per hour across the whole project** (not per address). If a first code landed in spam and you clicked \"send\" again, subsequent attempts get rejected — the app surfaces that as the rate-limit message, so watch for that when retrying.\n3. **Slow delivery.** The built-in mailer can take 1–3 minutes; it's not instant.\n\n## Quick check (10 seconds)\n\nSupabase dashboard → **Authentication → Users**:\n- If your email is listed (status \"waiting for verification\") → the send went out; it's a spam/delay issue → look in spam.\n- If it's **not** listed → the send failed or was rate-limited → wait ~10 minutes, then try once.\n\n## The real fix — make email reliable\n\nThe built-in mailer is explicitly not for production. Wire a proper one (~10 min, free tier works):\n\n1. Create a free account at **Resend** or **Brevo**, grab an API key.\n2. Supabase dashboard → **Project Settings → Authentication → SMTP Settings** → toggle \"Enable Custom SMTP\" → paste the sender (e.g. Resend: SMTP `smtp.resend.com`, port 465, user `resend`, pass = API key).\n3. Done — every 6-digit code after that arrives in seconds, reliably.\n\nThis is worth doing before your demo walkthrough anyway, since the reviewer signing up will hit the same rate limits.\n\n**While you're in that dashboard** — two other one-click items I'm waiting on: run `scripts/supabase-schema.sql` in the SQL Editor (makes the account sync live), and add the Google OAuth client for the \"Continue with Google\" button + real calendar bookings."}
